highest share across the three years.\n\nConverting to percentage terms reveals 0.499% for 2011, which is marginally higher than previous years. When rounding to three decimal places, the maximum value remains consistent at 0.005.\n\nI'll verify my calculations carefully to ensure precision in the final determination.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_f339c318c8df4a5abf9260b8","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Data from Treasury Bulletin for calendar year end values\n\n# 2009 (from 2011_03 page 59)\ntotal_liabilities_2009 = 4479544  # Total liabilities to all foreigners (in millions)\ncanadian_dollars_2009 = 17694    # Canadian dollar liabilities (in millions)\n\n# 2010 (from 2012_03 page 58)\ntotal_liabilities_2010 = 4640601\ncanadian_dollars_2010 = 15907\n\n# 2011 (from 2013_03 page 60)\ntotal_liabilities_2011 = 4925045\ncanadian_dollars_2011 = 24579\n\n# Calculate share (decimal) for each year\nshare_2009 = canadian_dollars_2009 / total_liabilities_2009\nshare_2010 = canadian_dollars_2010 / total_liabilities_2010\nshare_2011 = canadian_dollars_2011 / total_liabilities_2011\n\nprint(f\"2009: {share_2009:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"2010: {share_2010:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"2011: {share_2011:.6f}\")\n\n# Maximum share\nmax_share = max(share_2009, share_2010, share_2011)\nprint(f\"\\nMaximum share: {max_share:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"Rounded to 3 decimal places: {round(max_share, 3)}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
